{"book":32,"chapter":3,"context":{"chapter":3,"title":"Nineveh Repents","summary":"Given a second chance, Jonah preaches a brief warning in Nineveh; the whole city, from the king down to the animals, fasts and repents, and God relents from the disaster he had threatened.","background":"Nineveh is called 'an exceeding great city of three days' journey' (v. 3); whether that describes its size with surrounding towns or the time needed to visit it is debated. Jonah's message is only five words in Hebrew. The king's decree hopes God may still 'turn and repent' (v. 9), the same hope Joel offered Israel.","customs":[{"term":"Sackcloth and ashes","verses":"3:5-8","note":"Rough goat-hair clothing and sitting in ashes were public signs of grief and repentance. Even the animals wear sackcloth."}],"watchFor":["'The word of the LORD came unto Jonah the second time' (v. 1).","'The people of Nineveh believed God' (v. 5).","'God repented of the evil' (v. 10): his warnings invite repentance."],"connections":["Jeremiah 18:7-8","Joel 2:13-14","Matthew 12:41","Luke 11:30-32"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it came"],["דְבַר","devar-","H1697","HNcmsc","[the] word of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["יוֹנָה","yonah","H3124","HNpm","Jonah"],["שֵׁנִית","shenit","H8145","HAofsa","a second [time]"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"]],"x":[[32001001,32001001,4]],"xn":1},"2":{"w":[["קוּם","kum","H6965","HVqv2ms","arise"],["לֵךְ","lekh","H1980","HVqv2ms","go"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["נִינְוֵה","ninveh","H5210","HNpl","Nineveh"],["הָעִיר","ha'ir","H5892","HTd/Ncfsa","the city"],["הַגְּדוֹלָה","hagedolah","H1419","HTd/Aafsa","<the> great"],["וִּקְרָא","vikra'","H7121","HC/Vqv2ms","and call out"],["אֵלֶיהָ","'eleiha","H413","HRd/Sp3fs","against it"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["הַקְּרִיאָה","hakeri'ah","H7150","HTd/Ncfsa","the proclamation"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["